        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Name of the cell array that tells the faces of the mesh apart: one id for the wall, one for each cap, and 0 for the volume elements. This is what a solver reads the boundary conditions off, and it is also what holds the wall and the caps apart while the surface is remeshed. If the input surface already carries an array of this name - Clip Vessel writes its face labels into &quot;ModelFaceID&quot; - its ids are kept and any new caps are numbered above them; under any other name the faces of the input are renumbered from scratch.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="text">
         <string notr="true">CellEntityIds</string>
        </property>
        <property name="SlicerParameterName" stdset="0">
